{"symbol": "to_key_val_list", "type": "function", "file": "src/requests/utils.py", "lines": [335, 361], "source": "def to_key_val_list(value):\n    \"\"\"Take an object and test to see if it can be represented as a\n    dictionary. If it can be, return a list of tuples, e.g.,\n\n    ::\n\n        >>> to_key_val_list([('key', 'val')])\n        [('key', 'val')]\n        >>> to_key_val_list({'key': 'val'})\n        [('key', 'val')]\n        >>> to_key_val_list('string')\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n        ...\n        ValueError: cannot encode objects that are not 2-tuples\n\n    :rtype: list\n    \"\"\"\n    if value is None:\n        return None\n\n    if isinstance(value, (str, bytes, bool, int)):\n        raise ValueError(\"cannot encode objects that are not 2-tuples\")\n\n    if isinstance(value, Mapping):\n        value = value.items()\n\n    return list(value)", "calls": [], "called_by": [], "confidence": 0.92, "purpose": "Take an object and test to see if it can be represented as a"}
